        "content": "Kaunsa Better\r\nComparison:\r\nFactor Old Regime New Regime\r\nBasic exemption ₹2.5L ₹4L\r\n87A rebate (zero tax) Up to ₹5L income Up to ₹12L income\r\nDeductions (80C etc.) Allowed Most NOT allowed\r\nStandard deduction ₹50,000 ₹75,000\r\nTax rates Higher slabs Lower slabs\r\nRule of Thumb for Students:\r\nAgar aap 80C mein invest kar rahe ho (SIP , PPF, FD)  → Old Regime\r\nbetter hai kyunki deductions se taxable income kam hoti hai.\r\nAgar koi investment nahi ho rahi  → New Regime better hai kyunki lower\r\ntax rates hain + higher exemption.\r\nCalculator Example with ₹6 lakh salary:\r\nOld Regime: ₹6,00,000 - ₹50,000 (standard) - ₹1,50,000 (80C ELSS) = ₹4,00,000\r\ntaxable. Tax = ₹7,500. 87A rebate = ₹7,500. Tax = ZERO!\r\nNew Regime: ₹6,00,000 - ₹75,000 = ₹5,25,000 taxable. Tax = ₹6,250 (₹4L ke\r\nupar 5%). 87A rebate (up to ₹12L) = ₹6,250. Tax = ZERO!\r\nDono mein zero tax. Lekin agar 80C mein ₹1.5 lakh invest kiya → Old regime mein\r\nhabit bani + wealth create. New regime mein no investment = no wealth.\r\nDecision Flowchart:\r\nKya 80C mein invest kar rahe ho?\r\n    ↓ YES → Old Regime (deductions + lower taxable income)\r\n    ↓ NO → Kya income ₹12L se kam hai?\r\n        ↓ YES → New Regime (lower rates, no deductions needed)\r\n        ↓ NO → Calculate both, jo kam tax de wo lo\r\nCalculator:  incometax.gov.in pe free calculator available. Dono compare karo.",
